/-!
# The cut points of `_int_free` (PLAN.md G3, `free`)

The 4 cut points: the entry and where two ways meet. From each, the blocks up to the next cut points as one piece
(`W_*`, with its `Sp`, `c_*`): a block's straight-line code, then at its jump's exits the next block's condition, or `Q`
at a cut point or at an offset the proof does not go past (163, 341, 516, 566, 571, 576, 580, 683, 736, 743, 752, 759,
871, 880, 884, 903, 948, 977, 1056, 1278, 1455, 1527, 1606, 1745, 1784, 1840, 1855, 1891, 1911, 1929, 1963, 2008, 2061,
2073, 2113, 2149, 2176, 2234, 2274, 2308, 2341, 2372, 2403, 2434, 2439, 2470, 2501; the `ret`). `Wt` is the table of the
cut points' conditions, `spAll` its `Sp`s, for `Seg.cfg`. Generated by `tools/blk_gen.py`.
-/
namespace FV7z.Ifr
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
open ZellicX86 Decode FV7z.Leaf

def W_82 (fb : Addr) : Wpt := fun F Wl Q => wp F Wl o3 fun g f V =>
    (f.cond 5 = true → Q 752 g (rfz f) V) ∧
    (f.cond 5 = false → Q 90 g (rfz f) V)
theorem c_82 (prof : Profile) (fb : Addr) : SpF prof ifr ifr_at fb 82 (W_82 fb) :=
  SpF.blk_then (blk_82 prof) (SpF.jcc_then (spj_84 prof fb) (SpF.skip 752) (SpF.skip 90))

